SOURCE AVAILABILITY (MPL-2.0 section 3.2)
-----------------------------------------
The exact recipe that produces this binary is published at

    https://github.com/quickpod/quick-mail

and consists of:

  * pin.txt      the precise upstream release this is built from
                 (thunderbird 140.13.0esr), with the source tarball URL; the
                 tarball is verified against upstream's published SHA256SUMS
                 before use.
  * patches/     every modification made to MPL-covered files, as a script that
                 applies them by exact-string match and fails loudly if upstream
                 has moved, so the patch set can never silently drift.
  * branding/    Quick Mail's own branding directory.
  * mozconfig    the build configuration.
  * build.sh     the build itself.

Modifications made to MPL-covered files remain under the MPL-2.0.

WHAT WAS CHANGED FROM UPSTREAM
------------------------------
  * Product identity (name, profile location, application basename) rebranded
    to Quick Mail, as the trademark terms require.
  * OAuth2 client registrations are read from preferences, so Quick Mail
    presents its own registrations rather than Mozilla's. Upstream's source
    explicitly asks that its client IDs not be reused.
  * All automatic network activity in the default configuration removed: the
    remote start page and the in-app notification poller are disabled and
    unpointed, and the Health Report service is not compiled in. Quick Mail
    does not contact any server unless you configure a mail account or click a
    link. There is no auto-updater; updates arrive through the AIQuick apt
    channel.

THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
----------------------
The Thunderbird source tree vendors a large number of third-party libraries,
each retaining its own license. Their notices are preserved inside the source
tree and are reproduced in the application under "About Quick Mail".
